PR review on Ihorog/ci-moment-v2

Review comment:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

When logging an event, upserting the session with `created_at: receivedAt` will overwrite the session's original creation timestamp on conflict. Since multiple events are logged throughout a session, this continuously advances the session's `created_at` time, corrupting session analytics.

To fix this, omit `created_at` from the upsert payload and use `ignoreDuplicates: true` so that existing sessions are not modified, while new sessions still get created with the default database timestamp.

```typescript
    const { error: sessionError } = await supabase.from("ci_sessions").upsert(
      {
        id: sessionId,
        source: getText(payload, "source"),
      },
      { onConflict: "id", ignoreDuplicates: true },
    )

