PR review on CodeHalwell/AnimaOS

Review comment:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The query percent-encoding logic encodes UTF-32 code points (`c as u32`) directly instead of percent-encoding the UTF-8 bytes of non-ASCII characters.

For example, a non-ASCII character like `中` (U+4E2D) will be incorrectly encoded as `%4E2D` instead of its standard UTF-8 percent-encoded form `%E4%B8%AD`. This will cause SearXNG to fail to decode non-ASCII queries.

To fix this, iterate over the bytes of the query string instead of its characters.

```rust
        let encoded_query: String = query
            .bytes()
            .map(|b| {
                if b.is_ascii_alphanumeric() || b == b'-' || b == b'_' || b == b'.' || b == b'~' {
                    (b as char).to_string()
                } else if b == b' ' {

