PR review on patflynn/cosmo

Review comment:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

When `pollFallback` is enabled (e.g., on corp machines), the Tailscale webhook relay (`classic-laddie`) is unreachable. Leaving `relay_url` configured will cause `klaus` to repeatedly attempt connections to the unreachable relay, leading to unnecessary timeouts, connection errors, and log spam.

We can conditionally omit `relay_url` from the generated JSON configuration when `pollFallback` is active using `lib.optionalAttrs`.

```
      webhook = {
        port = 9800;
        path = "/webhook/github";
        poll_fallback = config.cosmo.klaus.pollFallback;
        secret_file = "/run/agenix/github-webhook-secret";
      } // lib.optionalAttrs (!config.cosmo.klaus.pollFallback) {
        relay_url = "https://classic-l

PR review on bashasnoglu-jpg/SANTIS_SITE

Review comment:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

In `showToast`, calling it multiple times quickly causes race conditions where older timeouts clear newer toast messages prematurely. Store the timeout ID in a ref and clear any existing timeout before scheduling a new one.

```javascript
  const toastTimeoutRef = useRef(null);

  const showToast = React.useCallback((title, message) => {
    if (toastTimeoutRef.current) {
      clearTimeout(toastTimeoutRef.current);
    }
    setToastMessage({ title, message });
    toastTimeoutRef.current = setTimeout(() => {
      setToastMessage(null);
      toastTimeoutRef.current = null;
    }, 4000);
  }, []);
```

