feat(inbox): return typed deterministic InboxSnapshot before rendering

> *This was generated by AI during triage.*

Blocked by: #104

## Outcome

Separate deterministic inbox collection from presentation by introducing a typed `InboxSnapshot` before rendering or prompting the LLM.

## Why

The current collector returns rendered text sections. That makes it hard to provide multiple UX surfaces: compact dashboard, detailed evidence, JSON/porcelain output, and LLM prompt input. A typed snapshot makes the deterministic pull reusable and testable.

## Proposed shape

Introduce an internal structure similar to:

```ts
interface InboxSnapshot {
  generatedAt: string;
  scope: {
    cwd: string;
    repo?: string;
    user?: string;
    forge: InboxForge;
    focus: InboxFocus;
  };
  status: "success" | "partial" | "failed";
  collectors: Array<{
    name: "github" | "gitlab" | "local" | "sessions";
    status: "ok" | "partial" | "skipped" | "failed";
    gaps: string[];
    commands: string[];
  }>;
  items: InboxItem[];
}
```

Exact names can change, but the deterministic collector should produce data first and strings second.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Add `collectInboxSnapshot(...)` or equivalent typed collector.
- [ ] Preserve `collectInboxEvidence(...)` as a compatibility wrapper while renderers migrate.
- [ ] Track per-collector status, gaps, and read-only commands.
- [ ] Add a JSON/porcelain rendering path for deterministic tooling or future dashboard use.
- [ ] Existing inbox tests still pass after migration.
- [ ] New tests assert snapsho

