Feature Request: Permit Readonly arrays in `Provider`

### Which @angular/* package(s) are relevant/related to the feature request?

`@angular/core`

### Description

Sometimes it's useful to have a shared set of providers that get imported together:

```ts
export const SERVICE_PROVIDERS = [
  ServiceA,
  ServiceB,
  // ...
]
```
```ts
@Component({
  // ...
  providers: [SERVICE_PROVIDERS],
})
// ...
```

This pattern is subject to really confusing issues if someone does something like `SERVICE_PROVIDERS.push(...)`, so it would be better if I could use a type annotation to avoid mutating the array, i.e.:

```ts
export const SERVICE_PROVIDERS: readonly Provider[] = [
  ServiceA,
  ServiceB,
  // ...
]
```

However, adding the annotation triggers a build-time error and requires an update to the component definition:
```ts
@Component({
  // ...
  providers: [...SERVICE_PROVIDERS],
})
// ...
```
This technically impacts runtime performance by duplicating the array at runtime (just to satisfy the type requirements at build time).

It is a pretty minor concern, but declaring that arrays passed as `Provider` are readonly both offers a small performance win _and_ provides a TS-based assurance that the provided array will not be mutated by the framework (which I sure hope is true!).

### Proposed solution

Update `Provider` type to accept `readonly any[]` instead of `any[]`:

https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/255151a41349c519728651739412dbd0f6138e13/packages/core/src/di/interface/provider.ts#L336-L343

